# Run Typecheck After TS Changes

After changing `.ts` or `.tsx` files, run `npm run typecheck` before considering the task done.

- Do not treat `next dev` or "Compiled successfully" as type-safe. Vercel production builds run a full TypeScript check and will fail on errors the dev compiler misses.
- If typecheck fails, fix the errors before finishing.
- Control-flow narrowing is a common miss: after `if (value) { return }`, `value` is narrowed (often to `null`). Do not use `value?.prop` in that branch.

```tsx
// BAD — weekInfo is already null here; optional chaining types as never
if (weekInfo) {
  return inSeasonWeeks
}
weeks.filter(w => isPreseasonVisibleInApp(weekInfo?.weekType))

// GOOD — off-season branch does not read weekInfo
if (weekInfo) {
  return inSeasonWeeks
}
weeks.filter(w => w.weekType !== 'preseason')
```
